# Internationalization (i18n) System

## Supported Languages

- **Bengali (bn)**: Primary language (Flow is Bengali-first)
- **English (en)**: Secondary language
- **Hindi (hi)**: Tertiary language (future expansion)
- **Arabic (ar)**: Tertiary language (future expansion)

## File Structure

```
lib/l10n/
├── app_bn.arb                    # Bengali translations (primary)
├── app_en.arb                    # English translations
├── app_hi.arb                    # Hindi translations (future)
├── app_ar.arb                    # Arabic translations (future)
├── app_localizations.dart        # Main localization class
├── app_localizations_bn.dart     # Bengali implementation
├── app_localizations_en.dart     # English implementation
├── app_localizations_hi.dart     # Hindi implementation (future)
└── app_localizations_ar.dart     # Arabic implementation (future)
```

## Usage Patterns

### 1. Basic String Access
```dart
// Get localized strings
final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context);
Text(l10n.welcomeTitle)           // "Welcome to Flow" / "Flow-এ স্বাগতম"
Text(l10n.appTitle)               // "Flow"
Text(l10n.tagline)                // "Money in Motion, Life in Balance" / "টাকার flow, জীবনের balance"
```

### 2. Common UI Strings
```dart
// Action buttons
AppButton(
  text: l10n.save,
  onPressed: () {},
)

AppButton(
  text: l10n.cancel,
  style: AppButtonStyle.outline,
  onPressed: () {},
)

// Dialog text
AppDialog(
  title: l10n.confirm,
  content: l10n.deleteConfirmation,
  actions: [
    AppButton(text: l10n.yes, onPressed: () {}),
    AppButton(text: l10n.no, onPressed: () {}),
  ],
)
```

### 3. Form Labels and Hints
```dart
AppTextFormField(
  label: l10n.amount,
  hintText: l10n.enterAmount,
  validator: (value) => value?.isEmpty == true ? l10n.required : null,
)

AppTextFormField(
  label: l10n.note,
  hintText: l10n.addNote,
)
```

### 4. Navigation and Headers
```dart
CustomAppBar(
  title: l10n.dashboard,
  subtitle: l10n.welcomeBack,
)

AppListTile(
  title: l10n.transactions,
  subtitle: l10n.viewAllTransactions,
)
```

## Locale Management

### 1. Locale Provider
```dart
// Watch current locale
final locale = ref.watch(localeProvider);

// Change locale
ref.read(localeProvider.notifier).setLocale(Locale('bn'));

// Toggle between languages
ref.read(localeProvider.notifier).toggle();
```

### 2. Locale Notifier Usage
```dart
class MyWidget extends ConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final locale = ref.watch(localeProvider);
    final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context);
    
    return Column(
      children: [
        Text(l10n.currentLanguage),
        ElevatedButton(
          onPressed: () {
            ref.read(localeProvider.notifier).toggle();
          },
          child: Text(l10n.changeLanguage),
        ),
      ],
    );
  }
}
```

## Cultural Intelligence Patterns

### 1. Bengali-First Approach
```dart
// Always provide Bengali translation first
class CulturalLocalizations {
  static String getGreeting(Locale locale, DateTime time) {
    final hour = time.hour;
    switch (locale.languageCode) {
      case 'bn':
        if (hour < 12) return 'সুপ্রভাত';
        if (hour < 17) return 'শুভ দুপুর';
        if (hour < 20) return 'শুভ সন্ধ্যা';
        return 'রাতের শুভেচ্ছা';
      case 'hi':
        if (hour < 12) return 'सुप्रभात';
        if (hour < 17) return 'नमस्ते';
        if (hour < 20) return 'शुभ संध्या';
        return 'शुभ रात्रि';
      case 'ar':
        if (hour < 12) return 'صباح الخير';
        if (hour < 17) return 'مساء الخير';
        if (hour < 20) return 'مساء النور';
        return 'ليلة سعيدة';
      default:
        if (hour < 12) return 'Good morning';
        if (hour < 17) return 'Good afternoon';
        if (hour < 20) return 'Good evening';
        return 'Good night';
    }
  }
}
```

