### 3. Empathetic Messaging
```dart
// Use empathetic, non-judgmental language
class EmpatheticMessages {
  static String getOverBudgetMessage(String category, Locale locale) {
    switch (locale.languageCode) {
      case 'bn':
        return '${category} এ একটু বেশি খরচ হয়েছে। কোনো সমস্যা নেই—কখনো কখনো হয়।';
      case 'hi':
        return '${category} में थोड़ा ज्यादा खर्च हुआ है। कोई बात नहीं—कभी-कभी होता है।';
      case 'ar':
        return 'أنفقت أكثر قليلاً على ${category}. لا بأس—يحدث أحياناً.';
      default:
        return 'You spent a bit more on ${category} this time. No worries—it happens.';
    }
  }
}
```

## Translation Key Patterns

### 1. Naming Conventions
- Use snake_case for keys: `welcome_title`, `add_transaction`
- Group related keys with prefixes: `cat_`, `btn_`, `msg_`
- Use descriptive names: `welcomeTitle`, `deleteConfirmation`

### 2. Common Key Patterns
```dart
// UI Actions
l10n.save, l10n.cancel, l10n.delete, l10n.edit
l10n.back, l10n.next, l10n.skip, l10n.finish
l10n.continuee, l10n.retry, l10n.confirm

// Navigation
l10n.dashboard, l10n.transactions, l10n.wallets, l10n.categories

// Forms
l10n.amount, l10n.note, l10n.date, l10n.category
l10n.enterAmount, l10n.addNote, l10n.selectCategory

// Messages
l10n.success, l10n.error, l10n.warning, l10n.info
l10n.loading, l10n.noData, l10n.tryAgain

// Categories
l10n.cat_food_dining_name, l10n.cat_transport_name
l10n.cat_shopping_name, l10n.cat_rent_name
```

