## Best Practices

### 1. Always Use Localized Strings
```dart
// ❌ Don't hardcode strings
Text('Welcome to Pocketa')

// ✅ Use localized strings
Text(l10n.welcomeTitle)
```

### 2. Handle Missing Translations
```dart
// The system will fallback to English if Bengali translation is missing
Text(l10n.someKey) // Will show English if Bengali not available
```

### 3. Use Context for Locale Access
```dart
// ❌ Don't access locale directly
final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context);

// ✅ Use in build method
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  final l10n = AppLocalizations.of(context);
  return Text(l10n.welcomeTitle);
}
```

### 4. Test Both Languages
Always test your app in both English and Bengali to ensure:
- All strings are translated
- UI layout works with longer/shorter text
- RTL support if needed (for future languages)

### 5. Use Meaningful Key Names
```dart
// ❌ Unclear keys
l10n.msg1, l10n.btn1, l10n.text1

// ✅ Clear, descriptive keys
l10n.welcomeMessage, l10n.saveButton, l10n.errorTitle
```